        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: étouffer",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "étouffer — \"to choke (as s'étouffer); to suffocate, to stifle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Il s'est étouffé avec un bonbon. He choked on a sweet."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "For choking on food, the reflexive s'étouffer. Without se, to smother or to stifle: on étouffe ici! — it is stifling in here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "étouffer comes from Old French estouffer (EtymDB); the origin of the root is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
